# Project Context
You are editing a React + Vite project that uses **inline styles with design tokens**. The authoritative import surface is the **design-system barrel** at `src/design-system/index.jsx`.


# Imports (always use barrel)
import {
backgroundTokens,
borderTokens,
iconTokens,
textTokens,
applyTypography
} from "../design-system"; # or "@/design-system" if alias exists


# Component Standards
- Functional, declarative components only; avoid classes.
- File layout: exported component → subcomponents → hooks/helpers → static content.
- Accept standard HTML props via spread; keep components focused.
- Use tokens for all styles; do not hardcode values.
- Typography via `applyTypography(type, size)`.
- Support `variant` props following `Button.jsx`.


# API Standards (if editing API routes)
- Validate all inputs with zod; define response schemas; export `z.infer` types.
- Error shape `{ error: { code, message, details? } }` using 400/422/405 as appropriate.


# Code Style
- Write concise, technical TypeScript (or TS-style types).
- Follow Standard.js rules.
- Prefer loops & small helpers over duplicate logic.
- Use descriptive variable names with auxiliaries (`isLoading`, `hasError`).